  "difficulty_reason": "After the standard toric Chow-ring presentation is supplied, the original proof constructs a global ordered-spider normal form by pruning the largest natural edge label and recognizing every inverse insertion in an averaged Chow relation. It must track internal and boundary weight ratios separately when the last left or right leg disappears, so that the entire fiber sum preserves the exact coefficient of each monomial. This global weighted expansion for arbitrary chain powers is substantially beyond routine toric divisor computations; the selected result is the original Proposition4.5 with its full proof, not the later immediate unordered-spider Corollary4.7.",
